works: It takes a cold month and two awkward talks, but the line is settled and the hellos come back, stiffly.
works: The quarrel ends with a new fence or a trimmed hedge, and a nod across it that both sides can live with.
fails: Letters go back and forth for a season, and every time {N} pulls into the drive the curtain next door twitches.
fails: The hedge comes down or it stays, and either way {rival} stops speaking, and the whole street picks a side.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- show_rivalry (cycle s2)

== the prize table at the town show
tier: life event
land: show_rivalry
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-90
per_year: 0 0 .25 .25 .25 .25
tone: mixed
life: nature, leisure
horizon: week
roles: rival, group, neighbour, friend, elder
with: rival, group
earth: the town's produce and flower show in the hall, long tables of entries, and a rival grower two places down
tribal: the gathering where the season's best roots and fruit are laid out, another grower's basket heaped beside the next
magic: the autumn show below the tower, where an enchanted ribbon drifts to the winner, and a rival grower knows too much about charms
scene: The hall smells of sweet peas and damp earth, and the long tables are lined with onions, dahlias and marrows, each on its plate with a card. {Ns} entry sits two places down from the grower who has won three years running, and the judges are working their way along the row.
scene W: The rules are pinned up by the door, and they are very particular about stalk length.
scene U: {Ns} onions came out well this year, but the winner's are bigger, and {N} wants to know how.
scene B: The cup has the winners' names engraved round the base, going back decades, and {Ns} is not on it.
scene R: The judge has a cousin among the entrants, everyone knows it, and nobody says it.
scene G: Most of what {N} grew this year has already been eaten at the kitchen table, and it was very good.
scene with rival: {rival} has beaten {N} three years running, and always says so kindly. Today {rival} leans over to straighten {Ns} card, just a little too helpfully.
scene with group: {group} have entered as a team this year, a whole table of their plot's best, and they are anxious about the beans. They keep looking at {N} as if {N} might know what the judges like.
scene tribal: At the gathering the season's best roots and fruit are laid out on skins for all to see. Another grower's basket sits beside {Ns}, heaped higher, and the elders walk slowly along the line.
scene magic: At the autumn show below the tower an enchanted ribbon drifts along the tables and settles on the winner. The champion grower has been seen at the hedgewitch's door twice this month, buying something.
- W | enter by the rules to the letter, and shake the winner's hand whoever it is | land: W | v: conformity, tradition | lever: loyalty | opens: allotment | foot: place gather.hall | chance: 75
- U | save seed from your best and breed a better one for next year | land: U | v: achievement, self-direction | lever: voice | opens: regen_farming | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 65
- B | win this time, whatever it takes | land: B | v: power, achievement | lever: subvert | foot: door kept it hidden | chance: 55
- R | challenge the judge out loud about the cousin on the entry list | land: R | v: self-direction, stimulation | lever: voice | foot: mark defied an authority | chance: 50
- G | skip the show this year, since the garden is for eating, not for prizes | land: G | v: universalism, hedonism | lever: exit | foot: means time+.03 | chance: 85
- W>B | join the show committee and get the rule on stalk length changed | land: W | v: conformity, power | lever: found | foot: place rule.counsel | chance: 55
- B>G | offer the winning grower a fair price for a handful of their seed | land: B | v: achievement, benevolence | lever: fund | foot: person friend | chance: 65
- G>U | ask the oldest grower in the hall how it was done in their day, and listen | land: G | v: tradition, self-direction | lever: voice | foot: person elder | chance: 80
- U>R | enter something nobody has shown before: an odd old kind no one can name | land: U | v: self-direction, stimulation | lever: found | foot: lesson strange entries get remembered | chance: 55
- R>W | laugh off the loss, buy the winner a cup of tea, and mean it | land: R | v: benevolence, hedonism | lever: loyalty | foot: person rival lost | chance: 70
works: The card says second again, but the winner shakes {Ns} hand properly this time, and it feels almost as good.
works: A rosette goes on {Ns} plate, and {N} carries it home past the whole street, trying not to grin.
fails: The judges pass {Ns} entry without a pause, and the walk home is a long one.
fails: Words are said by the tea urn that cannot be unsaid, and next year's show already feels like a feud.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- remembrance_tree (cycle s1)

== the path they used to walk
tier: life event
land: remembrance_tree
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
when: an adult kin has died; a place they loved outdoors
tone: mixed
life: nature, family
horizon: years
roles: parent, grandparent, sibling, partner, child
with: kin, alone
earth: the hill path someone loved, walked again in the weeks after they have gone
tribal: the high rock above the camp where the one who died used to sit, climbed again after the mourning
magic: the grove below the tower where the one who died used to walk, where the old trees are said to remember
scene: {dead} walked this path most mornings for years, and now {N} walks it without them. The bench is still there, the view is still there, and the wind still comes up the valley the way it always did.
scene W: There is nothing up here to say {dead} was ever here, and {N} thinks there should be.
scene U: {N} keeps thinking about time: how long the hill has been here, and how long anything lasts.
scene B: There is a sign on the field gate below the path: land for sale, building plans applied for.
scene R: {N} wants to do something loud, something {dead} would have laughed at.
scene G: The grass is moving on the hill the way it moved when {dead} was alive, and the larks are up.
scene with kin: {N} and {with} walk up together, not saying much, the way {dead} would have walked it with either of them. At the top {with} sits on the bench and says, "This was always the spot."
scene with alone: {N} comes up alone, early, before anyone else is about. The path is wet, and there is nobody to be brave for.
scene tribal: {N} climbs to the high rock above the camp where {dead} used to sit and watch the herds. After the mourning the place feels too big, and the wind too loud.
scene magic: In the grove below the tower, where {dead} used to walk, the old trees are said to remember every footstep. {N} stands among them and listens, just in case.
- W | ask the council for a bench on the path, with {dead}'s name on a plate | land: W | v: tradition, benevolence | lever: voice | foot: means money-.03 | chance: 70
- U | plant a young oak there, a tree that will outlive every one of you | land: U | v: universalism, tradition | lever: loyalty | foot: place prod.wild | chance: 75
- B | put in an offer on the field below, so no one can ever build there | land: B | v: power, security | lever: exit | foot: means money-.10 | chance: 50
- R | climb to the top of the hill and shout {dead}'s name into the wind | land: R | v: stimulation, self-direction | lever: subvert | foot: means freedom+.03 | chance: 75
- G | scatter the ashes where {dead} used to walk, and let the wind take them | land: G | v: tradition, universalism | lever: loyalty | foot: lesson grief walks easier outdoors | chance: 80
- W>U | walk the path on the same day every year, and note what has changed | land: W | v: tradition, self-direction | lever: loyalty | foot: door kept your word | chance: 80
- U>B | gather {dead}'s favourite walks into a small guide, sold for the people who cared for them | land: U | v: benevolence, achievement | lever: fund | foot: place care.houses | chance: 55
- B>R | organise a sponsored run up the hill in {dead}'s name, and run it first | land: B | v: achievement, stimulation | lever: lead | foot: means health+.03 | chance: 60
- R>G | swim once in the cold pool below the path, where {dead} used to swim | land: R | v: stimulation, tradition | lever: exit | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 65
- G>W | bring the family up each spring to tidy the path and share {dead}'s stories | land: G | v: tradition, benevolence | lever: loyalty | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 75
works: Months later {N} walks the path and finds it lighter, as if {dead} had made room.
works: The family comes up together on the anniversary, and for the first time the talk is more laughing than crying.
fails: The walk only makes it worse today, and {N} turns back before the top, the path too full of {dead}.
fails: The plan falls through, the bench or the plot or the tree, and {N} feels they have let {dead} down.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- first_date_outdoors (cycle s2)

== the first afternoon by the lake
tier: life event
land: first_date_outdoors
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
when: a new romance; a lake, a park or a beach
tone: joy
life: nature, love
horizon: moment
roles: partner
with: partner
earth: a first day out with someone new, by the lake in the park, with the whole afternoon ahead
tribal: a first walk out with someone new, down to the lake below the camp, with the afternoon ahead
magic: a first day out with someone new, at the lake below the tower where the swans are said to be enchanted
scene: It is a bright afternoon by the lake, and {N} and someone new are still at the stage of choosing every word. Boats are tied up at the jetty, there is an island in the middle with one tree on it, and the grass slopes down to the water.
scene W: {N} has packed a proper picnic: a cloth, real plates, something homemade.
scene U: There is so much {N} wants to ask, and a rowing boat would mean an hour with no interruptions.
scene B: {Ns} family has a field on the hill above the lake, with the best view for miles.
scene R: The island is not that far, and the water looks warm enough.
scene G: The grass is long and soft, and there is no hurry about anything.
scene with partner: {with} turns up a little late and a little nervous, holding a paper bag from the bakery. They walk down to the water side by side, close but not quite touching.
scene tribal: {N} walks down to the lake below the camp with someone new, both of them pretending not to notice the others watching. The reeds are tall, and the afternoon is long.
scene magic: At the lake below the tower the swans are said to be enchanted, and to bow to new sweethearts. A swan glides past {N} and the newcomer without bowing, and they both laugh.
- W | lay out a proper picnic, planned down to the napkins | land: W | v: tradition, benevolence | lever: loyalty | foot: means time-.02 | chance: 80
- U | row out on the lake and talk about everything, with no one to interrupt | land: U | v: self-direction, stimulation | lever: loyalty | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 75
- B | take {with} up to the view from your family's land above the lake | land: B | v: power, security | lever: exit | foot: place prod.land | chance: 65
- R | swim out to the island together, laughing the whole way | land: R | v: stimulation, hedonism | lever: exit | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 60
- G | lie back in the long grass and see who talks first | land: G | v: hedonism, universalism | lever: neglect | foot: lesson silence can be easy | chance: 80
- W>B | book a table at the lakeside cafe ahead, so the day goes exactly to plan | land: W | v: conformity, achievement | lever: lead | foot: means money-.03 | chance: 70
- B>G | bring a basket of food you grew yourself, and let it say what words cannot | land: B | v: achievement, universalism | lever: voice | foot: lesson homegrown food speaks plainly | chance: 70
- G>U | walk slowly along the shore and name the birds for {with}, one by one | land: G | v: universalism, self-direction | lever: voice | foot: place prod.wild | chance: 75
- U>R | find the hidden cove you know of, where nobody else ever goes | land: U | v: self-direction, stimulation | lever: exit | foot: door kept it hidden | chance: 65
- R>W | ask {with} straight out, before the day ends, to come again next week | land: R | v: stimulation, benevolence | lever: voice | foot: door kept your word | chance: 65
works: The afternoon goes by in what feels like ten minutes, and they are still talking when the park keeper rings the closing bell.
works: Walking back, their hands find each other without either of them deciding it, and neither lets go.
fails: The clouds come over and the wind gets up, and the day ends early with wet shoes and polite goodbyes.
fails: The talk never quite catches, and they part at the gate with a "maybe again soon" that neither of them is sure about.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- storm_night_together (cycle s1)

== the night of the storm
tier: life event
land: storm_night_together
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-90
per_year: 0 .25 .25 .25 .25 .25
tone: mixed
life: nature, home
horizon: moment
roles: parent, sibling, grandparent, child, neighbour, group, elder
with: kin, group
earth: a winter storm at night, the power out, and the household or the street gathered in one candlelit room
tribal: a storm in the night, and the band crowded together in the big shelter while the wind tears at the hides
magic: a storm in the night that rattles the tower's shutters, and the whole lane gathered in the one cellar with a fire
scene: The storm arrives after dark and bangs at the windows for an hour, and then the power goes. The house fills up: the household, and soon a couple of neighbours too, everyone in the one room with a candle and the hiss of rain on the glass.
scene W: There are candles in the drawer and blankets in the cupboard, and nobody has thought to fetch them.
scene U: The old wind-up radio still works, and there is a forecast on the hour.
scene B: Something hit the roof a minute ago, and it sounded very much like {Ns} roof.
scene R: Down at the harbour the boats are knocking against the quay, and the moorings were never meant for this.
scene G: The wind is very loud and the room is very warm, and the youngest is asking for a story.
scene with kin: {N} and {with} sit under one blanket, counting the seconds between flash and thunder the way the family always has. Each time it comes closer, they both laugh, a little too loudly.
scene with group: {group} have ended up in the one house with a gas stove, and the kettle has been on all night. Somebody has brought cards, somebody has brought a dog, and nobody is going home until it blows over.
scene tribal: The storm comes in the night and the band crowds into the big shelter while the wind tears at the hides. Someone builds up the fire, and {elder} begins to talk.
scene magic: A storm rattles the tower's shutters all night, and the whole lane gathers in the one cellar with a fire. The old ones say it is the sky's old quarrel with the sea, and pour the tea.
- W | share out the candles and blankets so everyone in the room has some | land: W | v: benevolence, conformity | lever: loyalty | foot: mark helped someone in need | chance: 85
- U | keep the radio on all night and track the storm on a scrap of paper | land: U | v: self-direction, security | lever: neglect | foot: lesson storms pass in bands | chance: 75
- B | check your own roof and windows before helping anyone else | land: B | v: security, power | lever: exit | foot: means ties-.02 | chance: 75
- R | head down to the harbour and tie the boats down before the worst of it | land: R | v: stimulation, benevolence | lever: subvert | foot: mark took a wild risk | chance: 55
- G | tell stories by candlelight until the storm passes | land: G | v: tradition, benevolence | lever: loyalty | foot: means ties+.04 | chance: 85
- W>U | take charge of the torches and the first-aid box, and know where everything is | land: W | v: conformity, security | lever: lead | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 75
- U>B | fill every pan and the bath with water before the taps fail, and take the credit | land: U | v: security, achievement | lever: lead | foot: means ties+.02 | chance: 70
- B>R | get everyone guessing the minute the lights come back, and keep the score | land: B | v: stimulation, hedonism | lever: lead | foot: person friend | chance: 75
- R>G | open the back door a crack and watch the storm tear through the trees | land: R | v: stimulation, universalism | lever: exit | foot: means freedom+.02 | chance: 80
- G>W | gather everyone into the one warm room and keep the old songs going | land: G | v: tradition, benevolence | lever: loyalty | foot: place gather.house | chance: 80
works: By dawn the wind has dropped, and the street comes out blinking to count slates and share what is left in the kettles.
works: Years later it is still the storm night everyone talks about: the candles, the stories and the dog that slept through all of it.
fails: The roof leaks over the landing, nobody sleeps, and the morning shows a fence down and a long clean-up ahead.
fails: The power stays off for two days, the food in the freezer spoils, and the cold gets into everyone's temper.
